    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42829" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scālāris</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a flight of steps</i>
			or <i>a ladder</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">forma,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5,
					6 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">STRVCTIO,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4570</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scālārĭa</span></b> ,
				ĭum, n., <i>a
				flight of stairs</i> or <i>steps</i>, <i>a staircase</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5, 6,
				3</span></i>; also in the sing.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">SCALARE, is,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4750</span></i>
			.</div>
